<title>FINLAND: Finnair to start flying Helsinki-Dublin.</title>
<headline>Finnair to start flying Helsinki-Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national carrier Finnair Oy said on Thursday it will start three weekly regular scheduled flights between Helsinki and Dublin on May 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Finnair's Dublin flights, via Stockholm, will be flown in a code-share partnership with Irish airline Aer Lingus.</p>
<p>The Dublin flights will be on Tuesdays, Thursdays and Sundays, Finnair said in a statement.  </p>
<p>&quot;The flight is the only direct connection between Stockholm and Dublin,&quot; Finnair said.</p>
<p>It will fly to and from Dublin with a 122-seat DC-9-50 aircraft.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
